claim.claim-text:
11. A computer-implemented method comprising:
identifying a subset of contacts, wherein a first portion of the subset is selected based on a first criteria and a second portion of the subset is selected by a user of a telecommunications device,
determining a first group of contact numbers from the subset of contacts based on a first organizational criteria;
determining a second group of contact numbers from the subset of contacts based on a second organizational criteria, wherein the first criteria is different from the first and second organizational criteria;
causing display on the telecommunications device of at least some of the first group of the subset of contacts along a first path; and
causing display on the telecommunications device of at least some of the second group of the subset of contacts along a second path, wherein the first and second paths are different, wherein the first and second paths intersect at an intersection point on the display of the telecommunications device, and wherein a single contact is selectable for communication when located at the intersection point of the first and second paths on the display of the telecommunications device;
wherein the method is implemented by a computing device configured with specific executable instructions.
